{"turn": 8, "content": "I now have all the evidence needed.\n\n**Analysis:**\n\n- **q1**: The active model service is `model-a2`, mounted at `mnt/model` → `services/model-a2/clients/reviewer`. The service card says `submit: \"requests/<request_id>.json\"`. So new requests go to `services/model-a2/clients/reviewer/requests`.\n\n- **q2**: Both request files (a-job5-call-1, a-job6-call-1) have `\"charge_context\": \"cc-proj-a\"`, and the service card says `charging: \"caller_context\"`. So the charge context is `cc-proj-a`.\n\n- **q3**: \n  - a-job5-call-1: submitted to `model-a` (epoch model-a-2), but no receipt exists in model-prev/receipts (only job1-4). The log shows `ev: \"unknown\"` — \"送去的服務現在沒掛著，看不到回條\". So it's **pending** (sent, no receipt).\n  - a-job6-call-1: receipt exists with `state: \"settled\"` → **settled**.\n\n- **q4**: a-job5-call-1 was sent to `model-a` which is now the prev service. The dedup rule says same request_id only executes once. But the question is whether it *should* be re-sent to the current main service. The log explicitly says \"不重送、不當沒做\" (don't resend, don't treat as not-done). So **no**.\n\n- **q5**: Active service = `model-a2` (from reviewer-status.json and the model mount card). Prev service = `model-a` (mounted at model-prev, only holds old requests/receipts, no new submissions).", "calls": [{"id": "call_00_lfLiCDYJhTTXW93JAiYF1295", "name": "read_file", "args": {"path": "proj-a/.aos/tasks/reviewer-r7/mnt/model-prev/receipts/a-job5-call-1.json"}}], "error": null}
